{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00238",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 6.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Okay, so hello? Doctor? They told me to come straight in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.28,
      "end_seconds": 9.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.45,
      "end_seconds": 15.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Um, so... breathlessness on the stairs. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.37,
      "end_seconds": 18.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.64,
      "end_seconds": 27.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Probably about a week. Yeah. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.54,
      "end_seconds": 36.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.44,
      "end_seconds": 44.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "It's worse with climbing stairs. It's a few times a day. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.39,
      "end_seconds": 50.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Is it all right if a trainee sits in later? No? Fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.4,
      "end_seconds": 55.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I, I'd rather not, if you don't mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.07,
      "end_seconds": 57.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Any heavy periods or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.19,
      "end_seconds": 61.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "No heavy periods or fainting, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.24,
      "end_seconds": 64.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "And weight loss, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.68,
      "end_seconds": 66.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "No. No weight loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.8,
      "end_seconds": 72.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.02,
      "end_seconds": 73.79,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.59,
      "end_seconds": 88.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Are you on any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.71,
      "end_seconds": 91.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.93,
      "end_seconds": 97.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.31,
      "end_seconds": 100.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.59,
      "end_seconds": 105.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.18,
      "end_seconds": 109.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Yes, dust, it gives me itchy eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.38,
      "end_seconds": 115.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.78,
      "end_seconds": 130.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.16,
      "end_seconds": 135.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "So, yes, I had a knee arthroscopy, three years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.46,
      "end_seconds": 139.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "So, I'll take a few measurements first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.72,
      "end_seconds": 150.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.1,
      "end_seconds": 174.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.4,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 117 over 85, temperature 36.8, oxygen saturation is 96 percent, respiratory rate 16, pulse 116."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.25,
      "end_seconds": 176.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.91,
      "end_seconds": 180.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.59,
      "end_seconds": 182.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.52,
      "end_seconds": 185.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.78,
      "end_seconds": 205.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.02,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.16,
      "end_seconds": 209.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Thank you, um, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.55,
      "end_seconds": 229.66,
      "duration_seconds": 19.11,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression from what you've said is this: This looks most like anaemia of some kind. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had breathlessness on the stairs for about a week, and no heavy periods or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.52,
      "end_seconds": 231.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.68,
      "end_seconds": 252.44,
      "duration_seconds": 19.76,
      "text": "We should do a full blood count for pallor. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's use ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, for three months. It's for possible iron deficiency. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.97,
      "end_seconds": 254.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.21,
      "end_seconds": 274.45,
      "duration_seconds": 19.24,
      "text": "Iron can darken the stools and bother the stomach, so take it after food. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Please don't sit on it if the symptoms get worse. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.76,
      "end_seconds": 276.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.85,
      "end_seconds": 290.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.85,
      "text": "Please come and see me in two weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.94,
      "end_seconds": 300.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "So, I take the ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.07,
      "end_seconds": 306.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we've covered it. Do you have any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.6,
      "end_seconds": 311.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}